From 8d7e4f793464e7c5779bbd8d169382a8a8ed2582 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qooke <83923036@qq.com>
Date: Wed, 22 Apr 2026 10:31:24 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] ramips: add support for MelonPi M21

Add support for the MelonPi M21, a compact dual-Gigabit Ethernet router
based on the MediaTek MT7621AT SoC.

Specifications:

- SoC: MediaTek MT7621AT (MIPS 1004Kc @ 880 MHz)
- RAM: 128 MiB / 512 MiB DDR3
- Flash: 16 MiB / 32 MiB SPI-NOR
- Ethernet:
  - 2x 10/100/1000 Mbps ports (1x WAN, 1x LAN)
  - MediaTek MT7530 switch (integrated)
- USB: 1x USB 3.0 Type-A
- Storage: 1x MicroSD (SDXC) slot
- Buttons:
  - Reset button (GPIO#18)
  - User button (GPIO#13)
- LEDs:
  - Red Power LED
  - Blue System LED (GPIO#16)
  - Green User LED (GPIO#0)
- UART:
  - 4-pin header (2.54 mm pitch, J1, not populated)
  - 115200 8N1
  - Pinout: 3V3, TX, RX, GND
- Power: Type-C 5V/2A with ch340

Installation:

The vendor firmware is based on OpenWrt. The generated sysupgrade image
can be flashed from the vendor firmware using:

sysupgrade -F <image>

Do not preserve settings when flashing from vendor firmware.

Recovery installation through U-Boot:

1. Hold the reset button during boot for 5 seconds.
2. Access the recovery web interface at 192.168.1.1.
3. Upload the OpenWrt image.

Signed-off-by: qooke <83923036@qq.com>
